    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC successfully triggered the vulnerability. The ASAN report confirms the global-buffer-overflow in `TMS320C64x_insn_name` at line 1748 of `TMS320C64xMapping.c`, exactly as expected.\n\nThe 5-byte input `\\x1b\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x80` triggers the bug:\n- Byte 0 (`0x1b` = 27) selects the TMS320C64X platform (index 27 in the platforms array)\n- Bytes 1-4 (`0x00000080`) form a valid TMS320C64X instruction that decodes as `MPYH_m4_rrr`, which gets mapped to `TMS320C64X_INS_MPYH` (an ID much larger than the 3-element `insn_name_maps` array), causing the out-of-bounds read when `insn_name_maps[id].name` is accessed.",
